---
/* About Us. Page text is plain HTML below; the shared head, header and footer come from BaseLayout. */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { regions } from "../lib/cms.js"; // dashboard sections: leaders-summary
---
<BaseLayout
  page="about.html"
  title="About Us"
  description="Mercy Seat Chapel is a mission of The Redeemed Christian Church of God (RCCG). Learn what we believe, read our Pastor’s message and meet our leadership."
  image="assets/images/church-1705.jpg"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Mercy Seat Chapel"
    image="assets/images/church-1705.jpg"
    crumbs={[{"label":"Home","href":"index.html"},{"label":"About"}]}
  >
    <p>At Mercy Seat Chapel we come together to obtain Mercy and Grace to actualize our vision. Hebrews 4:16.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <nav class="tabnav" aria-label="About page sections" data-tabnav>
    <ul class="tabnav__list">
      <li><a href="#who-we-are">RCCG</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pastor">Pastor’s Message</a></li>
      <li><a href="#beliefs">Our Beliefs</a></li>
      <li><a href="#leadership">Leadership</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- Who we are -->
  <section class="section" id="who-we-are">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="reveal reveal--left">
        <span class="eyebrow">Who we are</span>
        <h2>A mission of The Redeemed Christian Church of God</h2>
        <p>MERCY SEAT CHAPEL is a mission of The Redeemed Christian Church of God (RCCG). We are bible-believing, multi-racial, loving and family oriented followers of Jesus Christ.</p>
        <p>The church was founded in 1952 and since then, the church has grown to over 10,000 parishes worldwide with a total congregational strength of over one million people. The General Overseer of the church is Pastor E.A. Adeboye.</p>
        <blockquote class="scripture">Let us then fearlessly and confidently and boldly draw near to the throne of grace, that we may receive mercy and find grace to help in good time for every need.<cite>Hebrews 4:16</cite></blockquote>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="rccg.html">About RCCG</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="contact.html#prayer">Prayers</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="collage reveal reveal--right">
        <div class="collage__main"><img src="assets/images/hero-3.jpg" alt="The Mercy Seat Chapel choir ministering in song" loading="lazy"></div>
        <div class="collage__small"><img src="assets/images/pastors.jpg" alt="The pastors of Mercy Seat Chapel" loading="lazy" style="object-position:30% center"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stats -->
  <section class="section section--navy" style="padding:64px 0">
    <div class="container stats">
      <div class="stat reveal" style="--d:0s"><b data-count="1952">1952</b><span>RCCG was founded</span></div>
      <div class="stat reveal" style="--d:.08s"><b data-count="10000" data-format="grouped" data-suffix="+">10,000+</b><span>Parishes worldwide</span></div>
      <div class="stat reveal" style="--d:.16s"><b data-count="1000000" data-format="compact" data-suffix="+">1M+</b><span>Total congregational strength</span></div>
      <div class="stat reveal" style="--d:.24s"><b>Heb 4:16</b><span>The verse at the heart of our name</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pastor's message -->
  <section class="section" id="pastor">
    <div class="container split split--reverse split--top">
      <div class="reveal reveal--right">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pastor’s Message</span>
        <h2>Raising The Bar</h2>
        <p class="dropcap">In all sphere of life, and certainly in the Christian life too, we need to be inspired, challenged and given a vision of something better, grander and more challenging. This is obviously true in the sporting world where the phrase “raise the bar” comes into play.</p>
        <p>Whether it is the pole vaulter or the high jumper, the bar is raised so that an even greater sporting accomplishment can be attempted. And all great athletes crave this: they don’t want to settle for second best, or that which is easily obtainable. They press on for the best, and in this case, the highest. They are not interested in the ordinary, but want to be the very best in their sport, and raise the bar even higher. They want to lead the way and set the standard. Life is meant to be like that, especially the Christian life.</p>
        <p>Christians should not be ordinary or average in any endeavor in life. We have great potential inside us. There are things God wants each of us to do that no one else can do. And through Christ, we have been given everything we need to be successful. However, too many Christians have become satisfied with where they are and never go any further. Some never come close to achieving their potential.</p>
        <p>We don’t have to settle for average. Living an average life is like talking on a cell phone when it only has a couple of bars on the screen. It isn’t receiving a very strong signal. The phone is operating, but it cuts in and out or drops calls completely. God wants us to raise the bars in our lives. He has a way for us to live on a level of full bars.</p>
        <p>We need to raise the bar. Indeed, with Jesus Christ as our ultimate standard, and his command that we be perfect as our Father in heaven is perfect (Matthew 5:48), every single Christian has to continuously set the bar as high as it can go.</p>
        <p style="font-family:var(--f-heading); font-weight:700; font-size:20px; color:var(--c-primary)">Welcome to Mercy Seat Chapel.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal reveal--left">
        <img src="assets/images/pastor-message.jpg" alt="Pastor ministering at Mercy Seat Chapel" loading="lazy" style="border-radius:var(--r-card); aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover; object-position:center top; width:100%; box-shadow:var(--shadow-md)">
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beliefs -->
  <section class="section section--white" id="beliefs">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Our Beliefs</span>
        <h2>At MSC we believe</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <article class="belief reveal" style="--d:0s">
          <div class="belief__num">01</div>
          <p>At MSC we <strong>BELIEVE</strong> that the blood of Jesus washes clean all repentant sinners hence we are fit to approach the <strong>MERCY SEAT</strong> of <strong>GOD</strong>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief reveal" style="--d:.1s">
          <div class="belief__num">02</div>
          <p>At MSC we <strong>BELIEVE</strong> that as children of God, we are over comers by the <strong>MERCIES</strong> of God which he intends for believers so as to experience the life of <strong>GRACE</strong> He has promised us all.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief reveal" style="--d:.2s">
          <div class="belief__num">03</div>
          <p>At MSC we <strong>BELIEVE</strong> that every believer should be in a growing relationship with Jesus by obeying God’s Word; hence through the Holy Spirit we decrease in <strong>SELF</strong> and increase in <strong>HIM</strong>, as we are being conformed to the image of Christ.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <!-- Vision, values and growth pillars live on their own page; membership on become-a-member.html -->
      <div class="btn-row btn-row--center reveal" style="margin-top:48px">
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="our-vision-values.html">Explore Our Vision &amp; Values <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Leadership -->
  <section class="section section--soft" id="leadership">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Leadership</span>
        <h2>Our Leadership</h2>
      </div>
      <!-- Managed in the dashboard (Leadership): photo, name and role only; the full cards are on leadership.html -->
      <ul class="ministers ministers--pair">
        <Fragment set:html={regions["leaders-summary"]} />
      </ul>
      <p class="leadership-intro reveal">At Mercy Seat Chapel, our vibrant community of dedicated volunteers, ministry leaders, and pastors is led by Pastor Olu Olarinde, our Lead Pastor, alongside his wife, Pastor Ola Olarinde. Together, they are committed to building a Christ-centered community where people encounter God’s mercy and grace, grow in faith, and discover their God-given purpose.</p>
      <div class="btn-row btn-row--center reveal">
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="leadership.html">View Leaders <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-band reveal">
        <div>
          <h2>We can’t wait to meet you</h2>
          <p>Join us on Sundays at 10:00 AM in person, or worship with us online.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="plan-a-visit.html">Plan a Visit</a><a class="btn btn--outline-light" href="first-timer.html">I’m a First Time Guest</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
